WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W18 (0.2.4)


STATE

  Version 0.2.4, Phase P3 IN PROGRESS (line editor, history, job
  control, completion, and highlighting/suggestions complete), on
  branch dev. 0.2.4 adds:
  - live syntax highlighting in include/tam-clam/highlight.h and
    src/edit/highlight.c backed by the real parser (sh->silent_errors),
    with a 64-slot per-prompt command-existence cache and opt-out via
    TAM_CLAM_HIGHLIGHT=0 / NO_COLOR;
  - dimmed history ghost-text suggestions rendered in src/edit/render.c
    and accepted with Right (full) or Ctrl+Right / Alt+. (one word) at
    end of line in src/edit/edit.c (opt-out via TAM_CLAM_SUGGEST=0);
  - tests/test_highlight.c unit tests, live PTY highlight/suggestion
    tests in tests/pty/test_pty.c, and sandbox/demo-0.2.4-highlight.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


